cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "Lutetia: a synthetic multi-domain EnergyML reference model of the Paris Basin"
abstract: >-
  Lutetia is a synthetic EnergyML model (RESQML 2.2, EML 2.3, WITSML 2.1, PRODML 2.3)
  of the Paris Basin around the Louvre, built by a replayable recipe with the energyml CLI.
  It combines real boreholes of the BRGM subsurface databank with invented structures,
  logs and production data. It is a test and teaching model, not a geological study.
authors:
  - name: "Geosiris"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-28"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23730911"
repository-code: "https://github.com/geosiris-technologies/energyml-lutetia"
url: "https://www.geosiris.com"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"  # the data (LICENSE-data); the recipe and the scripts are under Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - EnergyML
  - RESQML
  - WITSML
  - PRODML
  - Paris Basin
  - synthetic data
  - reference model
